  Hilbert space

Generate all higher structure from the minimum
relational mechanism.

----------------------------------------
0. PRE-RELATIONAL SUBSTRATE
----------------------------------------

Type:

  Q□

Fundamentals:

  Q□ is not a set.
  Q□ is not a space.
  Q□ is not observable.
  Q□ is not relational.

Axiom:

  Any attempted closure reflects irrationality.

Operator:

  Reflection(Q□) -> C_Q

where

  C_Q := irreducible residue.

----------------------------------------
1. TRIAD GENERATOR
----------------------------------------

No stable dyads.

Rule:

  Dyad + C_Q -> Triad

Definition:

  T = (s,i,d)

Types:

  s : structure seed
  i : interaction seed
  d : dynamics seed

Fundamental object:

  T(s,i,d)

----------------------------------------
2. RELATIONAL GEOMETRY
----------------------------------------

Definition:

  G = (Obj,Rel)

Generated from triads:

  Obj := { T_a }

  Rel := admissible triadic couplings

No coordinates.

No locations.

No metric.

Only relations.

----------------------------------------
3. STRUCTURE LAYER
----------------------------------------

Type:

  S

Definition:

  S := closure-stable subrelations

Rule:

  S subset G

Interpretation:

  persistent relational skeleton

----------------------------------------
4. INTERACTION LAYER
----------------------------------------

Type:

  I

Definition:

  I := generated constraints on S

Rule:

  S subset I

